{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/derio-net/super-fr/pulls/523","id":4591761847,"node_id":"PR_kwDOR-_5V88AAAABEbC5tw","html_url":"https://github.com/derio-net/super-fr/pull/523","diff_url":"https://github.com/derio-net/super-fr/pull/523.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/derio-net/super-fr/pull/523.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/derio-net/super-fr/issues/523","number":523,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"chore(fr): tier the two remaining pre-tier plans (gh-434 follow-up)","user":{"login":"YiannisDermitzakis","id":10046982,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDQ2OTgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10046982?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis","html_url":"https://github.com/YiannisDermitzakis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YiannisDermitzakis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Follow-up to #506, which added the untiered-agentic-phase warning to `fr plan self-review`. Two plans predate `tier` and carried **14 untiered agentic phases** between them — 14 warnings on every self-review since.\n\n| Plan | agentic | tiers assigned |\n|---|---|---|\n| `2026-07-09-multi-backend-git-host-adapters` | 8 | 1 hard · 5 standard · 2 mechanical |\n| `2026-09-04-worktree-traceability` | 6 | 2 hard · 2 standard · 2 mechanical |\n\nManual phases correctly get none — they are never dispatched to a model.\n\n### Assignment reasoning\n\n`hard` went to the three phases whose difficulty is design rather than volume: multi-backend's phase 1 (cross-backend URL parsing and detection — the design all three adapters rest on), and worktree-traceability's phases 1–2 (a new data model plus per-session index, and the gc/staleness hygiene that later produced the #435/#467 reap data-loss bug). `mechanical` went to prompt genericization, scaffold flags, docs, and a single script with golden tests.\n\n### The gate fired on its own author\n\nAdding tiers under `fr_version: '>=3.0.0,<5.0.0'` immediately tripped the *other* gate #506 added — the floor probe — because a pre-3.12.0 `fr` cannot parse `tier` on a closed-world `PhaseHeader`. Both plans are floored at `>=3.12.0,<5.0.0`. Pleasing to have the check catch the person who wrote it.\n\n### Deliberately not fixed\n\nBoth plans still warn about a **missing walking-skeleton marker**. Pre-existing, predates the marker entirely, and picking a retroactive skeleton phase on a plan that may be mid-flight is the plan owner's judgment, not a housekeeping edit's. Flagging rather than silently choosing.\n\n### Verification\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `fr plan self-review` (both plans) | 0 tier warnings (was 14); exit 0 |\n| `fr validate artifacts` | 33 artifacts, all structurally valid |\n| `fr acceptance check` | 171 rows OK |\n| `pytest test_plan_tier_gates test_validate_artifacts` | 59 passed |\n\nNo version bump: `docs/**` only.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","created_at":"2026-09-21T13:00:44Z","updated_at":"2026-09-21T13:53:45Z","closed_at":"2026-09-21T13:53:44Z","merged_at":"2026-09-21T13:53:43Z","merge_commit_sha":"089fb51d177e2d57fde02af4b908e5a5b9f3ad5a","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repo